From c0606d6fc1c1dc36c7855a0300124d5acb925b03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Norton <gregory@serenade.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:12:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Lagom: Build TextEditor on host

The last app of the completion plan. Two wirings, both in the Lagom
library/app lists: add LibCMake to the standard libraries (a small pure
syntax-highlighting library that only links LibSyntax -- needed for
TextEditor's CMake highlighting), and add TextEditor itself to the host
applications list. All of its other link dependencies already build on
host -- LibMarkdown, LibGemini and LibSyntax are standard Lagom libraries
(the plan's assumption that they were missing was stale), and
LibWebView/LibFileSystemAccessClient came in with the browser stack and
the FileSystemAccessServer work. Its GML stringifies to a .cpp compiled
into the app, so no binary-dir include path is needed. The web view used
for markdown/HTML preview is created lazily, so a plain-text session needs
no WebContent; opening a file goes through
request_file_read_only_approved(), which auto-approves.
---
 Meta/Lagom/CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Meta/Lagom/CMakeLists.txt b/Meta/Lagom/CMakeLists.txt
index 687dc972bb..884a288afa 100644
--- a/Meta/Lagom/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Meta/Lagom/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -471,6 +471,7 @@ if (BUILD_LAGOM)
         Compress
         Config
         Crypto
+        CMake
         Cpp
         Desktop
         DeviceTree
@@ -595,6 +596,7 @@ if (BUILD_LAGOM)
         add_serenity_subdirectory(Userland/Applications/Piano)
         add_serenity_subdirectory(Userland/Applications/SoundPlayer)
         add_serenity_subdirectory(Userland/Applications/Terminal)
+        add_serenity_subdirectory(Userland/Applications/TextEditor)
 
         # Terminal's pty helper is declared as a second target of the Terminal
         # component; build it here so that target exists for the host build.
-- 
